<p>
I&rsquo;ve always had a thing about desks. I really enjoy looking at pictures of people&rsquo;s work areas and in particular their desks. I&rsquo;ve gone through stages. Sometimes I really liked <a href="https://a.1stdibscdn.com/19th-century-french-renaissance-desk-with-three-drawers-for-sale-picture-2/f_17262/f_372045321700651913397/IMG_1382_master.jpeg">renaissance desks</a>, sometimes <a href="https://a.1stdibscdn.com/british-colonial-style-ming-inspired-solid-mahogany-five-drawer-desk-20th-c-for-sale-picture-2/f_21653/1610049121490/Colonial_Desk_2_master.jpg">colonial desks</a>, and sometime <a href="https://img.foter.com/photos/title/modern-l-shaped-desks.jpg">modern desks</a>. Basically, I just want a table that can hold my computer, keyboard, and a few other work items.
</p>
<p>
Fatih Arslan has <a href="https://arslan.io/2025/11/18/my-two-part-desk-setup/">his own take on the matter</a>. Like me, he appears to prefer a desk that is basically a table but he has a unique view of how to use it. His idea is to have two desks in one. His physical desk is 200 cm long, which gives him a lot of room. The surprising thing is what he does with all that length.
</p>
<p>
He divides the desk into two parts. One half is the &ldquo;digital side&rdquo; where he has his computer, his keyboard, and little else. In order to earn a place on this side of the desk, something has to be used regularly for his writing, coding, or taking business calls.
</p>
<p>
The other half is the &ldquo;analog side&rdquo;. It&rsquo;s for things that don&rsquo;t need a screen. It has pens, notebooks, books he reading, and miscellaneous sheets of paper that he&rsquo;s working on.
</p>
<p>
The split makes perfect sense. One side&rsquo;s for computer tasks and the other side is for activities that don&rsquo;t require a computer. Arslan has been using the setup for about 10 months and it&rsquo;s working well for him.
</p>
<p>
There is, I think, something to be said for having space on your desk that&rsquo;s not taken up by a keyboard and on which you can write with a pen, read a book, or simply play with the kids.</p>
